  "key_findings": [
    "c=12: Cloud-9 causality requires sigma_peak in [30] cm^2/g. Cloud-9 floor requires sigma_peak in [75, 100, 125, 150, 174, 200, 250] cm^2/g. Intersection at c=12: EMPTY.",
    "c=4 (Ohana+ physical anchor): intersection at c=4 is [75, 100, 125, 150, 174, 200, 250]. At sigma_peak=174 (canonical): V_max=25.59, sigma/m(V_max)=120.35, t_core=4.9554 Gyr -- an 11% discrepancy from section 9.12's 4.42 Gyr (see finding 5 below for reconciliation), ratio=14.783.",
    "Fornax sigma_HL required: marginal (within 0.15 of zero) for sigma_peak in []; substantive (more negative) for [30, 50, 75, 100, 125, 150, 174, 200, 250]. The Fornax outlier ranges from (-0.39) at sigma_peak=30 to (-0.61) at sigma_peak=250.",
    "Phase 44 free fit (sigma_peak=196.3): sigma/m(28) = 190.73, sigma/m(c=12 V_max) = 185.74, sigma/m(c=4 V_max) = 138.23. Meets floor. At c=12: ratio=0.722 (below cap). At c=4: ratio=12.871 (OK).",
    "section 9.12 reconciliation: section 9.12 reports t_core = 4.42 Gyr at c=4 with sigma/m = 135.3 (the c=12 V_max sigma/m value). This sweep uses canonical self-consistent NFW at each c: at c=4, V_max = 25.59 km/s, sigma/m(V_max) = 120.35 cm^2/g (NOT 135.3, which was computed at V_max = 31.12, the c=12 value). With canonical sigma/m(V_max) = 149.99, the sweep computes t_core = 4.955 Gyr -- an 11% discrepancy from section 9.12's 4.42 Gyr. This 11% gap is NOT a match -- it is section 9.12's sigma/m being held constant at the c=12 value when applied to c=4, an internal inconsistency in section 9.12 that this sweep corrects. At c=12, the match IS exact (sweep t_core = 0.091 Gyr vs section 9.12's 91 Myr; sweep sigma/m(V_max=31.12) = 135.43 vs section 9.12's 135.3).",
    "Continuous intersection at c=12: [49.81, 57.24] cm^2/g (width ~7.43). Computed using exact 1/sigma_m scaling (ratio = K/sigma_m(V_max) with K constant ~134.0). Linear interpolation between grid points overestimates the crossing (gave [49.81, 59.49] = 9.67 wide); exact 1/sigma_m scaling gives [49.81, 57.24] = 7.43 wide. The qualitative finding (knife-edge window, not a single point) is unchanged. The window is NARROWER than my prior linear estimate: 7.43 cm^2/g wide instead of 9.67. This is the c-M tension at LambdaCDM-standard concentration in its sharpest form."
  ]
